he bug\n\nWhen the model is split across multiple GPUs using ```device_map=\"auto\"```, the liger-kernel will return a ```ValueError```.\n\n\n### Reproduce\n\n```import os\nos.environ['CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES'] = '0,1'\nfrom transformers import AutoModelForCausalLM, set_seed\nfrom transformers.loss.loss_utils import ForCausalLMLoss\nset_seed(0)\n\nfrom liger_kernel.transformers import apply_liger_kernel_to_qwen2\nimport torch\napply_liger_kernel_to_qwen2(\n    rope=True,\n    swiglu=True,\n    cross_entropy=False,\n    fused_linear_cross_entropy=False,\n    rms_norm=True\n)\nmodel = AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained(\"./Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct\",\n                                             torch_dtype=torch.bfloat16,\n                                             device_map=\"auto\")\nmodel.train()\ninputs={\n    'input_ids': torch.tensor([1]).unsqueeze(0),\n    'attention_mask':torch.tensor([1]).unsqueeze(0),\n    'labels': torch.tensor([2]).unsqueeze(0),\n}\nloss =model(**inputs).loss\n```\n\noutput:\n\n> ValueError: Pointer argument (at 0) cannot be accessed from Triton (cpu tensor?)\n\n### Versions\n\nPython version: 3.11.11\nLiger Kernel version: 0.5.4\nPyTorch version: 2.5.1+cu124\nCUDA version: 12.4\nHIP(ROCm) version: Not available\nTriton version: 3.1.0\nTransformers version: 4.49.0\nXPU version: XPU Not Available","closed_at":null,"comments":5,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/linkedin/Liger-Kernel/issues/593/comments","created_at":"2025-03-03T13:19:05Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/linkedin/Liger-Kernel/issues/593/events","html_url":"https://github.com/linkedin/Liger-Kernel/issues/593","id":2891235856,"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"total_blocking":0},"issue_field_values":[],"labels":[],"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/linkedin/Liger-Kernel/issues/593/labels{/name}","locked":false,"milestone":null,"node_id":"I_kwDOMgGs686sVMIQ","number":593,"performed_via_github_app":null,"pin